- If x ≡ 1 mod 3, then x² ≡ 1² = 1 mod 3.
- If x ≡ 2 mod 3, then x² ≡ 4 ≡ 1 mod 3 (since 4 - 3 = 1).

Wait, so if x is congruent to 1 or 2 mod 3, then x² is congruent to 1 mod 3. That's interesting. So regardless of whether a or b is 1 or 2 mod 3, their squares will be 1 mod 3. Therefore, if a and b are both not multiples of 3, then a² ≡ 1 mod 3 and b² ≡ 1 mod 3. Therefore, a² + b² ≡ 1 + 1 = 2 mod 3. So the remainder would be 2?

